 down their information so  I'm supposed to do that for every  item that we sell and that's not the end  of it under the second hand store  license owners must get fingerprinted  pay twice as much as a general business  license or face a fine of up to two  thousand dollars a day for  non-compliance and make no mistake when  DC is trying to stamp out business they  mean business Wednesday April fourth a  number of businesses in Adams Morgan and  also on U Street were visited by MPD the  Metropolitan Police Department along  with inspector from the department of  consumer of regulatory affairs or DCRA  they came in in a very aggressive way  and told them that they did not have the  right business license that they needed  a secondhand business license and they  said that they would be shut down if  they didn't get the right business  license within seven days merchants Mike  Moffat and business advocates like  Barton aren't taking it lying down they  pulled together and they're pushing back  it's never easy to fight city hall but  they're giving it their best shot and  after all they have nothing to lose but  their livelihoods it'll take a rewrite  of the other regulations we could do  that first by emergency legislation and  then you know hopefully by permanent  legislation so I mean it's going to take  some time but we've started the process  and we've got DC I raise attention so  we're hopeful it's it just seems like  just so heavy-handed that can easily  just just destroy businesses like what  we're pulling for you well thank you  good luck thanks  you
 

